# PurohitConnect Django

Mobile features go through `apps/api/` (`/api/v1/`). Keep payloads in `apps/api/serializers.py`. Reuse existing models; do not add a mobile-only database.

```python
# BAD — Flutter-only model or a second bookings table
class MobileBooking(models.Model): ...

# GOOD — serialize the existing Booking / Purohit
def purohit_payload(purohit, request=None, include_packages=False):
    ...
```

- CORS middleware (`apps.api.middleware.MobileApiCorsMiddleware`) stays first in `MIDDLEWARE` and must cover `/media/`.
- Detail endpoints may include gallery; list payloads stay lean.
- Local `ALLOWED_HOSTS` may be `*` so a phone on LAN can hit `:8001`.
- After API changes: `python manage.py test apps.api`.
- Match website copy and order (`apps/pujas/catalog.py` `CATEGORY_ORDER` / `PUJA_ORDER`) when the ticket is “like the website.”
